@* One finding, as both lists on the campaign page show it: how much it matters, where it is (a link
   to its field when the list gives one), what it says, and, for an amount outside one of her lines'
   range, the way to that range. Each part is its own element with a space between: Razor drops the
   space beside an @if, which ran the export list's parts together ("Worth a lookOffer › ..."), so
   the place's link or text is chosen inside its own span. *@
@* An LLM finding whose quote has left the form stays in its place, greyed and saying "Looks fixed"
   (owner, 2026-10-31, choice 5a), so the list keeps what is still to look at without a new run. *@
<li class="@ItemClass">
    @* What the LLM found says so beside how much it matters, "Worth a look · LLM" (owner,
       2026-10-10, option B: "letting them know probably won't hurt"; and "I prefer llm to ai"); a
       rule's finding carries no tag. The list's first such tag opens what "LLM" means (ExplainLlm);
       the rest are the word alone, so a list of them is not a row of buttons. Inside the label, so no
       space Razor drops beside the @if can run it into the place. *@
    <strong>@(Finding.Severity == Severity.Blocker ? "Must fix" : "Worth a look")@if (Finding.IsAi)
        {
            @(" · ")
            if (ExplainLlm)
            {
                <Llm TestId="@($"{Named}-ai-{Finding.SeenKey}")" />
            }
            else
            {
                <span data-testid="@($"{Named}-ai-{Finding.SeenKey}")">@Glossary.Llm</span>
            }
        }@if (LooksFixed)
        {
            @(" · ")<span data-testid="@($"{Named}-fixed-{Finding.SeenKey}")">Looks fixed</span>
        }</strong>
    <span class="muted">
        @if (JumpTo is { } jump)
        {
            <a class="muted" href="@jump">@Finding.Location</a>
        }
        else
        {
            @Finding.Location
        }
    </span>
    <span>@Finding.Message</span>
    @* A finding about one of her known lines' limits leads to that line on the Known items page,
       where its range is changed in place (owner, 2026-10-09: the caps "easy to find and update").
       The space before it is written out, as Razor drops the one beside the @if ("...(5%–10%).Change
       this line's range"). *@
    @if (FindingPlace.KnownLineLink(Finding) is { } link)
    {
        @(" ")<a class="caps-link" href="@link">Change this line's range</a>
    }
    @* A suggested fix (owner, 2026-10-31, answer 3b), where the list offers one (Fix) and the finding
       is not already fixed: the words, and "Use this", which changes the form only; or why not. *@
    @if (Fix is { } fix && Finding.Suggestion is { } suggestion && !LooksFixed)
    {
        <span class="suggestion">
            @(" ")<span data-testid="@($"{Named}-suggestion-{Finding.SeenKey}")">Suggested: "@suggestion"</span>
            @if (fix == FixOutcome.Applied)
            {
                @(" ")<button type="button" class="button" data-testid="@($"{Named}-use-{Finding.SeenKey}")" @onclick="() => Use.InvokeAsync(Finding)">Use this</button>
            }
            else
            {
                @(" ")<span class="field-help" data-testid="@($"{Named}-by-hand-{Finding.SeenKey}")">@(fix == FixOutcome.Fixed ? SuggestedFix.FixedText : SuggestedFix.ByHand)</span>
            }
        </span>
    }
</li>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public Finding Finding { get; set; } = null!;

    /// <summary>Where on the page its field is, or null to name the place without a link.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? JumpTo { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// What the list calls its findings, for their names on the page (data-testid): an LLM finding's
    /// tag is <c>{Named}-ai-{key}</c>, by its <see cref="Finding.SeenKey"/>, so the same finding in
    /// two lists on one page has two names.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Named { get; set; } = "finding";

    /// <summary>Whether this finding's "LLM" tag opens what LLM means: the list's first LLM finding's does.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool ExplainLlm { get; set; }

    /// <summary>An LLM finding carried from an earlier version whose quote is no longer in the form: shown greyed, "Looks fixed".</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool LooksFixed { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// What using its suggested fix would do (<see cref="SuggestedFix.Check"/>), in the list that offers
    /// fixes; null in a list that offers none, such as the warnings before export.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public FixOutcome? Fix { get; set; }

    /// <summary>"Use this": the page puts the suggestion into the form.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<Finding> Use { get; set; }

    private string ItemClass =>
        "finding " + (Finding.Severity == Severity.Blocker ? "blocker" : "warning") + (LooksFixed ? " looks-fixed" : "");
}
